From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:06:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] test(r65): the width-4 knee is width-locked, not a capacity -
 REFUTATION

The B working set per workgroup is NUM_COLS * k * 1.125. The knee at n=4 and
not n=3 on the published k=5120 column brackets any fixed capacity C in
[17.28, 23.04) KB with no fitting freedom, and that bracket puts the knee at
n=2 uniquely at k=10240 and k=12288. Both were pre-registered, with the rule,
before the run.

The knee does not move. Across k = 4096..12288 the n=3->4 step is 16.7 / 15.2 /
10.7 / 10.8 / 8.0 / 16.1 percent and the n=1->2 step never leaves the 5-9%
same-config spread. At k=12288 the working set at n=2 is 27.6 KB - past the
whole device's 32 KB of shared memory - and that step is +2.3%, while n=3->4 is
+16.1% at a working set of 55.3 KB, 2.4x the largest admissible C. A capacity
crossing cannot be width-locked across a 3x range of k.

The first round of this sweep ran only m=17408 and is kept as the negative
control that explains why: at 50 MB of A the dispatch is launch-bound, 34-38
GB/s-of-A flat, and the knee is not present to be moved. The m=248320 sweep
reads 78.8 GB/s at n=1, k=5120 against R61's published 79.5, which is the
validity gate the amendment asked for.

So four mechanisms are now falsified - register pressure (R50), instruction
count (R57), B traffic per output row (R50), and the B working set (here) -
and LDS staging is inapplicable because B is already read once per workgroup.
What is left is width-locked at four columns and k-independent, and the brief
says stop rather than build a fix for a mechanism that is not located.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-253 R65 MMVQ width knee, Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: op-level perf-mode only (rows in r65-evidence/22-ksweep-table.txt); served t/s UNMEASURED by the maker - HQ pairs quiet
Lane: lane-253
Cherry-picked-from: 694ae437c (SOURCE PATHS ONLY, ArifiLabs lane-254 R66 integration)
Recut-onto: 3df782d48 (ArifiLabs lane-254 R66c, from 97c8ca02d)
